  "grammar": {
    "title": "Adjective Agreement in Spanish",
    "explanation": "In Spanish, adjectives must agree in gender and number with the noun they describe:\n\n• Masculine singular: alto, bajo, viejo, guapo\n• Feminine singular: alta, baja, vieja, guapa\n• Masculine plural: altos, bajos, viejos, guapos\n• Feminine plural: altas, bajas, viejas, guapas\n\nAdjectives ending in -e (inteligente, amable, fuerte) or consonants (joven) do not change for gender, only for number: inteligente → inteligentes, joven → jóvenes.",
    "examples": [
      { "target": "La chica es alta y guapa.", "native": "The girl is tall and good-looking." },
      { "target": "Los estudiantes son inteligentes.", "native": "The students are intelligent." },
      { "target": "Mis abuelas son amables y fuertes.", "native": "My grandmothers are kind and strong." }
    ]
  },
